---
alwaysApply: false
globs:
  - "**/migrations/**"
  - "**/schema/**"
  - "**/*.sql"
  - "**/db/**"
  - "**/database/**"
  - "**/seed*"
---

========================
DATABASE RULES (Auto-applied to DB files)
========================

--- SCHEMA DESIGN ---
- Every table needs: id (primary key), created_at, updated_at
- Soft deletes preferred over hard deletes for user-facing data: add deleted_at
- Use enums for fixed-value fields (status, role, type) — never raw strings
- Index foreign keys and any column used in WHERE or ORDER BY clauses
- Avoid nullable columns unless NULL has a meaningful semantic difference from a default

--- NAMING CONVENTIONS ---
- Tables: snake_case, plural (users, subscription_plans, audit_logs)
- Columns: snake_case, singular, descriptive
- Indexes: idx_tablename_columnname
- Constraints: fk_tablename_referencedtable, uq_tablename_columnname
- RLS policies: tablename_operation_description (users_select_own_rows)

--- MIGRATIONS ---
Format every migration file header with:
```
-- Migration: [sequential number] [short description]
-- Created: [YYYY-MM-DD]
-- Description: [what this does and why]
-- Rollback: [instructions or "see rollback migration N+1"]
```

- Migrations are append-only in production — never edit an applied migration
- Test the migration on a copy of production data shape before applying
- Large data migrations (backfills) are separated from schema changes

--- RLS POLICY TEMPLATE ---
Always follow this pattern:
```sql
-- Enable RLS
ALTER TABLE table_name ENABLE ROW LEVEL SECURITY;

-- Policy: named, explicit, minimal
CREATE POLICY "policy_descriptive_name"
  ON table_name
  FOR [SELECT|INSERT|UPDATE|DELETE|ALL]
  TO authenticated
  USING ( auth.uid() = user_id )  -- read condition
  WITH CHECK ( auth.uid() = user_id );  -- write condition
```

- Write separate policies per operation (don't use ALL unless genuinely needed for all)
- Test each policy with a user who should NOT have access

--- PERFORMANCE ---
- No unindexed foreign keys
- Use EXPLAIN ANALYZE before finalizing any non-trivial query
- Pagination is required for any query that can return unbounded rows
